## Report
Attempted dynamic validation first. A debug build with `cargo test -p server-core --lib --no-run` failed because `ec-sys` requires the system library `libisal` (build.rs error: “libisal not found; install intel-isa-l or set PKG_CONFIG_PATH”). `valgrind` and `gdb` are not installed; `lldb` is present but no binary could be produced due to the missing dependency. Proceeded with code review. `begin_stream_part` enforces the 1..=10,000 part_number range (coordinator.rs:8088-8107). In contrast, `upload_part_copy` streams directly by calling `create_upload_part_stream_session` with the supplied part_number (coordinator.rs:11948-11972), and `create_upload_part_stream_session` stores `part_number` in `StreamUploadTarget::UploadPart` without validation (coordinator.rs:8135-8164). The authorization path for UploadPartCopy does not check the range; it only passes part_number into the SSE-C scope helper (authz.rs:2793-2858). `SseCustomerSegmentScope::multipart_part` only rejects zero or values that don’t fit in u16 (sse.rs:390-401), so 10,001 is accepted. This confirms the regression: UploadPartCopy bypasses the 10,000 upper bound and can store oversized part numbers.

